    "question": {
        "text": "§\n\nWhat ion channels are affected secondary to μ-opiate receptor stimulation?",
        "imageIds": []
    },
    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nWhat ion channels are affected secondary to μ-opiate receptor stimulation?\n\n(1) Open post-synaptic K+ channels\n(2) Close pre-synaptic Ca2+ channels\n\n(Stimulation of κ receptor in dorsal horn also ⇒ ↓ Substance P)\n\n[Image: 428dead22377897a9d417ee176ab7c9deb33c523e31d73daf2ae9959cc185676]\n\n[Image: 3a8c40e1bf331b56fd55adebef0c1f936f506d89266ee7fbdc70d5594c544eff]\n\n[Image: e56d105b91014f79c5ad0de8838bf922032459c54416e07ad6567030fac59747]\n\n2.3 - Opiates, naloxone, naltrexone\n[Image: 8c63f66e1475ebfbbcc015f86c45f70f27b9638bf47e69348646c4990296de78]\n\n[Image: b47e7d3b86bad869e7331d89f33ba683941084edc486d95ebd4f778abe30396e]\n\n[Image: cebffba4c7b60647cdca63b7244804bcbc7c40c622da192362fab73c599383a5]\n\n[Image: c9a40a799a9e26c6e31bb7c16bff7ac519064714902c043d5271f3647bb20264]\n\n[Image: b403693609b0867ce762c7ab20bd9fc9c104aa35e9f8acb51c112261b9e6c561]\n\n[Image: babd06a95abdbfef052b55ee0aa04d2c5fa4c0d57f5135a69bc03c1df2cdb4c8]\n\n[Image: d1c47228ae662cf96ec53d8fcd6db4c6e5d0c41085b5927065385642a583637d]\n\n[Image: b3b4a07988b21c6edd2197265fe818a572a63c7dc382d1a2c11a758bcfbb13ac]",
